          "source": "; Caesar cipher over the simulated UART. Letters rotate by +4; other bytes pass\n; through unchanged. ESC (byte 27) stops the loop. Ctrl-C stops the host process.\n;\n; Run with:\n;   uv run thor examples/uart-caesar-plus4.thor\n\nrot-upper == (lambda (byte)\n  (+ 65 (MOD (+ (- byte 65) 4) 26)))\n\nrot-lower == (lambda (byte)\n  (+ 97 (MOD (+ (- byte 97) 4) 26)))\n\nrot == (lambda (byte)\n  (if (AND (>= byte 65) (<= byte 90))\n      (rot-upper byte)\n      (if (AND (>= byte 97) (<= byte 122))\n          (rot-lower byte)\n          byte)))\n\nloop == (lambda (ignored)\n  (IO-BIND (UART-RX)\n    (LAMBDA (byte)\n      (if (= byte NIL)\n          (loop NIL)\n          (if (= byte 27)\n              (IO-RETURN NIL)\n              (IO-THEN (UART-TX (rot byte))\n                       (loop NIL)))))))\n\n(loop NIL)\n",
